WEBVTT

00:02.594 --> 00:03.962
GLORIA:
Whoa.

00:03.996 --> 00:08.567
This is so beautiful.

00:08.600 --> 00:10.202
Wow.

00:10.236 --> 00:12.104
That's a good price.

00:12.138 --> 00:13.839
Mom, can we leave soon?

00:13.872 --> 00:15.907
I'm tired.
I was at school all day.

00:15.941 --> 00:18.610
I don't know what you gonna do
when you get a real job.

00:18.644 --> 00:20.246
You said school is my job.

00:20.279 --> 00:21.513
Boy, shut up.

00:21.547 --> 00:22.848
I'm almost done.

00:22.881 --> 00:24.883
Wow.

00:24.916 --> 00:27.553
("Give Me One Reason"
by Tracy Chapman playing)

00:27.586 --> 00:30.522
* Give me one reason
to stay here *

00:30.556 --> 00:33.492
* And I'll turn
right back around *

00:37.363 --> 00:40.566
* Give me one reason
to stay here *

00:40.599 --> 00:44.002
* And I'll turn
right back around *

00:46.672 --> 00:50.509
* Said I don't want
to leave you lonely *

00:50.542 --> 00:54.646
* You got to make me
change my mind *

00:56.682 --> 00:59.385
* Baby, I got your number *

00:59.418 --> 01:03.055
* Oh, and I know
that you got mine *

01:06.392 --> 01:07.659
* But you know
that I called you... *

01:07.693 --> 01:08.994
Mom, can I get this shirt?

01:09.027 --> 01:10.862
-This one, in my hand.

01:10.896 --> 01:12.898
Better not have
no craziness on it.

01:12.931 --> 01:14.166
No.

01:14.200 --> 01:16.368
Oh, why you had
to pick this color?

01:16.402 --> 01:18.003
This is the only one.

01:18.036 --> 01:19.271
Let me see it.

01:19.305 --> 01:20.606
* Call me anytime... *

01:20.639 --> 01:21.707
Thanks, Mom.

01:21.740 --> 01:22.841
Oh, don't thank me yet.

01:22.874 --> 01:24.076
You're gonna work for it.

01:24.110 --> 01:26.212
Go and get me a bag
of potato chips.

01:26.245 --> 01:28.580
-The kind with the owl on it.

01:28.614 --> 01:31.183
Over there, by the jeans and
the socks and the other snacks.

01:31.217 --> 01:33.219
Go on and find it, boy.

01:56.908 --> 01:58.277
GLORIA:
Earn?

01:58.310 --> 02:00.312
You better be up, in there.

02:01.980 --> 02:04.850
I am.

02:04.883 --> 02:07.786
* Here comes
the brand-new flava in ya ear *

02:07.819 --> 02:10.256
* Time for new flava
in ya ear... *

02:33.745 --> 02:35.113
EARN:
What's up?

02:35.147 --> 02:37.383
Chillin'.

02:37.416 --> 02:38.984
Cool shirt.

02:39.017 --> 02:41.052
Thanks.

02:42.321 --> 02:44.390
You do the math homework?

02:44.423 --> 02:45.891
I forgot about it.

02:45.924 --> 02:48.294
Just copy it during lunch.

02:58.270 --> 03:00.406
Hey, who did that?

03:00.439 --> 03:03.209
Huh?

03:03.242 --> 03:05.177
I said, who did that?

03:08.146 --> 03:10.782
Aw.

03:18.857 --> 03:20.559
Hey, man, I'm sorry, though.

03:20.592 --> 03:21.960
-I didn't mean to...
-Yo.

03:21.993 --> 03:23.995
You threw that yogurt
out the window?

03:24.029 --> 03:25.397
Yeah, listen, I'm sorry.

03:32.638 --> 03:35.807
DRIVER:
No moving around the bus.

03:52.023 --> 03:55.126
BOY: Every single time, you're
always like, "No, stop it."

03:55.160 --> 03:58.163
:
That doesn't even make no sense.
-You know, you know.

03:59.197 --> 04:01.533
CHRIS:
Oh, snap.

04:01.567 --> 04:03.201
Look at the nigga
with the FUBU shirt.

04:03.235 --> 04:05.304
Yo, man, let me see.

04:06.738 --> 04:08.774
Man, do I want one of these.

04:08.807 --> 04:10.809
I got to wait
till my birthday, though.

04:10.842 --> 04:13.445
MARK: Oh, Earn out here,
he trying to jump fresh.

04:13.479 --> 04:14.846
I see you.

04:14.880 --> 04:17.015
You know.

04:17.048 --> 04:18.750
MARK:
Okay. I got you.

04:18.784 --> 04:20.352
So, what-what you telling me is,

04:20.386 --> 04:23.021
y'all finna be mad at me for
the rest of the time I'm here...

04:23.054 --> 04:24.823
Hey, Earn.

04:24.856 --> 04:25.924
I like your shirt.

04:25.957 --> 04:27.359
Thanks.

04:27.393 --> 04:29.094
It's new.

04:30.329 --> 04:32.130
MARK:
Wait, wait, wait.

04:32.163 --> 04:33.765
Y'all had a sale, or something?

04:33.799 --> 04:35.601
Why both y'all
got the same shirt?

04:36.868 --> 04:39.070
CHRIS:
Oh, shit!

04:39.104 --> 04:40.306
One of y'all got a fake shirt.

04:40.339 --> 04:43.008
Look, this one has more stripes

04:43.041 --> 04:45.243
than that one,
and that one got a patch.

04:45.277 --> 04:47.846
Oh, no, y'all wearing
fake FUBU now?

04:50.749 --> 04:51.750
My shirt ain't fake.

04:51.783 --> 04:53.885
Talk to Earn.

04:53.919 --> 04:55.220
My shirt ain't fake, either.

04:55.253 --> 04:56.388
"My shirt ain't fake, either."

04:56.422 --> 04:58.690
One of y'all got a fake shirt.

04:58.724 --> 04:59.791
Let me see the tags.

05:10.436 --> 05:13.071
-Same to me.

05:13.104 --> 05:15.206
CHRIS:
I don't think he's here yet.

05:15.240 --> 05:16.675
He wasn't on the bus,
so he might come late.

05:16.708 --> 05:18.677
Definitely gonna know
which one fake.

05:18.710 --> 05:21.413
MR. HALEY:
Okay, ladies and gents.

05:21.447 --> 05:23.949
Let's take our seats.

05:23.982 --> 05:26.418
I'm Mr. Haley, and I'm subbing

05:26.452 --> 05:28.587
for Mrs. Fox's homeroom.

05:28.620 --> 05:30.422
Why your shoes so dirty?

05:31.857 --> 05:33.224
He got chicken grease
on his shoes.

05:35.394 --> 05:37.295
Please take a seat, young man.

05:37.329 --> 05:39.598
Your underarms smell like ribs.

05:42.167 --> 05:44.970
Sit down right now.

05:50.141 --> 05:51.810
I'm gonna write you up.

05:51.843 --> 05:53.278
CLASS:
Oh...

05:56.815 --> 05:57.983
Earthquake!

06:14.533 --> 06:18.136
So, do you know why
you're here today, Alfred?

06:18.169 --> 06:20.606
Racism. Not everybody's
gonna like me.

06:20.639 --> 06:23.842
Well, no, that's not it.

06:23.875 --> 06:25.076
Waleed came here today
because he believes

06:25.110 --> 06:27.212
you stole
his graphing calculator.

06:27.245 --> 06:29.114
Hmm. Racism.

06:29.147 --> 06:31.149
He did steal my calculator.

06:31.182 --> 06:32.551
I know he did.

06:32.584 --> 06:34.386
-No, I didn't.
-He's lying.

06:34.420 --> 06:36.187
I bought one from him.

06:36.221 --> 06:38.056
It was the one that got stolen.

06:38.089 --> 06:39.625
My name was already
engraved in it.

06:39.658 --> 06:41.126
Prove it, 'cause that's a lie.

06:41.159 --> 06:42.528
This is exactly
why we don't allow

06:42.561 --> 06:43.829
the buying and selling

06:43.862 --> 06:45.797
of any items
here on school property.

06:45.831 --> 06:47.799
You definitely know
that, Alfred.

06:47.833 --> 06:49.334
I've told you that
several times.

06:49.367 --> 06:52.337
Well, if that was true,

06:52.370 --> 06:53.972
then both of us are guilty.

06:54.005 --> 06:56.542
You'd have to write me
and him up.

06:56.575 --> 06:59.277
So do what you got to do.

07:00.779 --> 07:03.849
Okay. Alfred, go back to class.

07:03.882 --> 07:06.151
And if I hear about
you selling anything,

07:06.184 --> 07:08.520
I'm gonna send you to I.S.S.
Got it?

07:08.554 --> 07:10.355
I need a pass.

07:12.891 --> 07:14.526
There you go.

07:28.640 --> 07:30.241
Hey, they got snitches
up in here!

07:30.275 --> 07:31.376
-MR. WHITMAN: Alfred!

07:31.409 --> 07:33.044
I will write you up, boy.

07:33.078 --> 07:35.080
Go to class!

07:40.218 --> 07:42.353
Wait, so what's going on?

07:42.387 --> 07:45.123
Devin has the exact
same shirt as me.

07:45.156 --> 07:47.125
Well, pretty much.

07:47.158 --> 07:48.426
One of 'em's bootleg, though.

07:48.460 --> 07:50.462
-Fake.

07:50.496 --> 07:51.597
So?

07:51.630 --> 07:53.331
Your shirt looks fine to me.

07:53.364 --> 07:55.433
But if it's fake,
everybody's gonna roast me.

07:55.467 --> 07:56.802
Forever.

07:56.835 --> 07:58.704
Remember how Thomas
got his nickname?

07:58.737 --> 07:59.871
Who?

07:59.905 --> 08:01.973
Thomas Jones.

08:02.007 --> 08:03.208
Doo-doo Jones.

08:03.241 --> 08:05.076
Oh. Yeah.

08:05.110 --> 08:07.078
Well, is your shirt fake?

08:07.112 --> 08:09.881
I don't know.

08:09.915 --> 08:13.585
Doesn't seem like
a big deal to me.

08:13.619 --> 08:15.420
I've worn this shirt
twice this week.

08:20.859 --> 08:22.828
Beat your ass
with your hand-me-down overalls.

08:31.402 --> 08:32.904
Gonna be major differences

08:32.938 --> 08:34.740
between animal cells
and plant cells.

08:34.773 --> 08:37.776
The cell walls, for instance.

08:37.809 --> 08:40.178
So, when we're looking
under the microscope,

08:40.211 --> 08:42.914
we are going to locate

08:42.948 --> 08:45.316
the key differences.

08:45.350 --> 08:46.518
Denisha.

08:46.552 --> 08:49.320
Denisha, sit up.
You can't sleep here.

08:49.354 --> 08:51.623
My head hurts.

08:51.657 --> 08:53.258
MRS. BANKS:
Remember you said you were going

08:53.291 --> 08:54.826
to do some work today?

08:54.860 --> 08:56.061
DENISHA:
So?

08:56.094 --> 09:00.666
Everybody, go ahead
and break into your lab groups.

09:03.835 --> 09:06.437
Denisha, do we need to go
and talk outside?

09:06.471 --> 09:07.673
No.

09:10.208 --> 09:12.177
We talked about this
at the meeting.

09:12.210 --> 09:14.479
Are we gonna have
a good day today?

09:14.512 --> 09:17.515
I don't know. Are we?

09:26.892 --> 09:28.794
This one's a plant cell.

09:28.827 --> 09:32.163
Are you sure? I couldn't tell.

09:32.197 --> 09:34.532
There's a chloroplast in there.

09:37.535 --> 09:41.740
Hmm, I thought that was
a mitochondria.

09:43.541 --> 09:44.976
You're pretty smart, Earn.

10:13.071 --> 10:15.506
RACHAEL:
Look at this one.

10:15.540 --> 10:19.510
The thing on the right
is a vacuole, right?

10:19.544 --> 10:22.648
I think so.

10:38.163 --> 10:39.564
Last one.

10:39.597 --> 10:42.600
Yeah? Let me see.

10:46.905 --> 10:49.340
You got a thread on your shirt.

10:49.374 --> 10:53.611
Um... it's an animal cell.

11:06.692 --> 11:09.060
All done.

11:38.423 --> 11:40.826
Hey, yo, is that him?
That's him. Come on, come on.

11:40.859 --> 11:42.093
-Come on, come on.
-Oh, sh...

11:42.127 --> 11:44.996
-Hold up, hold up, hold up.
-Yo, yo, yo.

11:46.464 --> 11:49.667
Oh, shit. Look at this.

11:49.701 --> 11:52.070
Nigga, where did you get
this fake

11:52.103 --> 11:53.404
A thrift store?

11:53.438 --> 11:55.907
My shirt's not fake.
I got it at a regular store.

11:57.843 --> 11:59.978
I don't...
My mom bought it for me.

12:00.011 --> 12:01.112
BOTH:
Oh!

12:01.146 --> 12:02.413
-Come here, come here.
-Hold on.

12:02.447 --> 12:04.415
Look at him trying to hide
his fake shirt.

12:04.449 --> 12:06.818
Don't try and hide that shit
now. It's too late, nigga.

12:06.852 --> 12:08.253
My shirt's not fake.

12:08.286 --> 12:10.655
Uh, I don't know, man.
It looks fake to me.

12:10.688 --> 12:12.891
Hey, this nigga
ain't got on FUBU.

12:12.924 --> 12:15.260
-He got "FEBE."

12:15.293 --> 12:18.663
Hey! Hey, everybody!

12:18.696 --> 12:22.167
-This man got on FEBE!

12:22.200 --> 12:25.236
Like, type of nigga to wear
four-line Adidas and shit.

12:48.359 --> 12:51.496
* Excuse me, do you think that *

12:51.529 --> 12:54.265
* I might be able
to touch you? *

12:54.299 --> 12:58.003
*
-* Yay-yay *

12:58.036 --> 13:00.505
* I can tell you how I feel *

13:00.538 --> 13:03.674
* About you night and day *

13:03.708 --> 13:05.543
* How I feel about you *

13:05.576 --> 13:08.346
* No, no *

13:08.379 --> 13:12.150
* I can tell you how I feel
about you... *

13:23.761 --> 13:25.230
What's up?
You got that homework?

13:25.263 --> 13:26.865
Left it in my locker.

13:28.399 --> 13:31.602
Everyone's talking about
you and Devin's shirt.

13:31.636 --> 13:33.538
Yeah, I know.

13:33.571 --> 13:35.273
People in other grades
know about it.

13:35.306 --> 13:36.707
Well, your shirt is real,

13:36.741 --> 13:39.210
so you ain't got
nothing to worry about.

13:39.244 --> 13:41.412
Everybody's gonna roast
the hell out of Devin, though.

13:41.446 --> 13:44.349
It's gonna be bad. You can't
wear no fake shit here.

13:44.382 --> 13:46.251
Nobody knows
whose shirt is fake.

13:46.284 --> 13:49.054
Johnny's not even here.

13:49.087 --> 13:51.289
Yeah, he is. He came in late,

13:51.322 --> 13:53.925
but he was in Ms. Wells' class
with me. He's here.

13:54.993 --> 13:57.062
OLDER KID:
This fool got on FEBE, too.

13:57.095 --> 13:59.998
Hey, look, look,
look, look, man.

14:00.031 --> 14:03.268
So, tell me, whose is fake,
yours or little dude over there?

14:03.301 --> 14:05.603
Man, my dad bought this for me.

14:05.636 --> 14:08.139
All right?
I don't wear bootleg clothes.

14:08.173 --> 14:10.641
I got all the Jordans,
everyone knows that.

14:10.675 --> 14:12.944
And Earn come in here every day
looking like a bum,

14:12.978 --> 14:15.146
so y'all know his shirt is fake.
Y'all know it.

14:15.180 --> 14:18.249
My dad don't buy me
nothing fake.

14:18.283 --> 14:20.886
: Hey,
you a funny dude, man, hold on.

14:20.919 --> 14:22.453
-Hey, come here, nigga.

14:22.487 --> 14:24.189
-Come on, brah.

14:24.222 --> 14:26.757
Why you got to be like that?

14:30.828 --> 14:33.965
Ooh, Rush Hour soundtrack.

14:35.833 --> 14:37.969
:
Al.

14:38.003 --> 14:41.239
Al. Alfred.

14:45.210 --> 14:47.946
Nothing, really.

14:47.979 --> 14:49.814
Hey, you saw that Dragon Ball Z
last night?

14:49.847 --> 14:51.682
Nah, my mom won't
let me watch it anymore.

14:51.716 --> 14:53.418
Saw the black guy
with the red lips

14:53.451 --> 14:55.320
and now she says it's racist.

14:55.353 --> 14:58.723
-Oh, yeah, man, that's weird.
-Yo. You got to help me.

14:58.756 --> 15:00.158
Why, what's wrong?

15:00.191 --> 15:02.193
It's my shirt.
Somebody has the same one as me

15:02.227 --> 15:04.362
and now everybody's saying
one of us has a fake shirt.

15:04.395 --> 15:06.264
Oh, snap, man, that's you?

15:06.297 --> 15:07.665
-Nothing.

15:07.698 --> 15:09.667
-I was trying to be cool.
-Bruh.

15:09.700 --> 15:11.836
Man, is this shirt bootleg?

15:11.869 --> 15:13.304
I don't know.

15:13.338 --> 15:16.141
I got it at Marshalls,
but it was on sale.

15:16.174 --> 15:18.176
Man, that's why you can't be
buying stuff on sale.

15:18.209 --> 15:19.644
Bro, you got to get some money.

15:19.677 --> 15:21.112
He's tripping.

15:21.146 --> 15:23.781
Look, there's a hole in it.

15:25.583 --> 15:27.986
I'm serious, Al.
I need your help.

15:28.019 --> 15:31.156
I'm not cool like you.

15:31.189 --> 15:34.159
If the older kids find me,
they're gonna beat me up.

15:34.192 --> 15:36.261
Yeah, man, you're right.

15:36.294 --> 15:37.996
What should I do?
I'm freaking out.

15:38.029 --> 15:40.731
Uh, how cool is the other kid?

15:40.765 --> 15:43.401
He's pretty cool.
He always has dope clothes.

15:43.434 --> 15:45.536
His dad is, like, 30.

15:45.570 --> 15:46.804
Man, don't be acting nervous.

15:46.837 --> 15:49.074
I mean, people try
to come at you, just deny it.

15:49.107 --> 15:50.141
Confidence is the key.

15:50.175 --> 15:52.877
All right?

15:52.910 --> 15:55.580
Hold it down, cuzzo.
Heading to lunch.

15:55.613 --> 15:57.615
Okay.

16:03.321 --> 16:05.023
MRS. WILLIAMS: Make sure
you finish your packets

16:05.056 --> 16:06.691
and bring them in tomorrow.

16:06.724 --> 16:08.726
I'm going to place a bin
on my desk.

16:08.759 --> 16:10.295
I want you to put them in there.

16:10.328 --> 16:12.230
And cite your work, folks.

16:12.263 --> 16:15.266
The Internet is not a source...

16:15.300 --> 16:16.901
-All right,

16:16.934 --> 16:18.769
names at the top
of your packets.

16:18.803 --> 16:22.373
That's an easy 50 points.
Good job.

16:37.722 --> 16:39.557
Wait, Earn!

16:39.590 --> 16:41.859
Johnny? Guess who I found.
Check it out.

16:41.892 --> 16:43.061
Oh, this shit crazy.

16:43.094 --> 16:44.929
Let me see the tag.

16:48.666 --> 16:50.435
This one's fake!

16:50.468 --> 16:51.736
It says "made in Bangladesh."

16:51.769 --> 16:52.803
It should be China.

16:52.837 --> 16:53.971
I knew he was wrong as hell.

16:55.673 --> 16:57.875
Hey, yo, his shirt fake, y'all!
Yo!

16:57.908 --> 16:59.777
Hold up, hold up,
hold up, hold up, hold on.

16:59.810 --> 17:01.112
Let me see.

17:08.153 --> 17:09.487
Let me see.

17:09.520 --> 17:11.756
Man, this one the real shirt.

17:11.789 --> 17:15.326
It's supposed to say "made in
Bangladesh" on this one.

17:15.360 --> 17:18.863
Of course this fool gonna say
"made in China." He is Chinese.

17:18.896 --> 17:20.898
-Come on, man.

17:20.931 --> 17:23.134
That one the fake one.
Trust me, I know.

17:24.802 --> 17:27.605
Man, my shirt ain't fake.
It ain't.

17:27.638 --> 17:29.140
CHRIS:
Yo, this nigga homeless!

17:29.174 --> 17:31.309
Devin rockin' fake FUBU now.

17:31.342 --> 17:33.344
JOHNNY:
I'm not Chinese. I'm Filipino.

17:50.061 --> 17:51.929
Wait. Here you go, Earn.

17:51.962 --> 17:54.199
You know, that's my number,
if you want to call me.

17:54.232 --> 17:55.366
But only between 6:00 and 9:00.

17:55.400 --> 17:56.601
O-Okay, cool.

17:56.634 --> 17:59.537
-See you tomorrow, Earn.
-See ya.

18:02.673 --> 18:05.976
Yo. I can't believe this fool
tried to lie on you.

18:06.010 --> 18:07.612
Yeah, it's crazy.

18:07.645 --> 18:09.080
Yeah, 12th-graders
just found out.

18:09.114 --> 18:10.715
They're going in on this man.

18:22.026 --> 18:24.229
-Damn.

18:24.262 --> 18:26.231
Hey, FEBE, man.

18:28.333 --> 18:30.668
OLDER KID: You finna cry
or something

18:45.950 --> 18:48.586
("Passing Me By" by The Pharcyde
playing)

18:48.619 --> 18:51.322
GIRL : Band practice
will be moving to Room G today

18:51.356 --> 18:53.090
due to a leak in the ceiling.

18:53.124 --> 18:55.092
That is Room G.

18:55.126 --> 18:57.695
Just a reminder,
the book fair is this Tuesday.

18:57.728 --> 18:59.497
If you have any books
you want to donate,

18:59.530 --> 19:01.966
you can trade them
with Mr. Johnson...

19:04.402 --> 19:05.370
Spirit Week is next week.

19:05.403 --> 19:07.738
We will be doing Pajama Day,

19:07.772 --> 19:10.575
Sports, Crazy Hair,
and '80s Day...

19:33.831 --> 19:36.100
Everyone, please settle down.

19:45.976 --> 19:49.914
I came to let you all know
something very serious.

19:49.947 --> 19:53.884
Your classmate, Devin Myers,
committed suicide last night.

19:56.687 --> 19:58.556
We're not sure why,

19:58.589 --> 20:01.091
but we've heard
a couple of things.

20:01.125 --> 20:03.928
It seems Devin's parents
had just gotten divorced,

20:03.961 --> 20:06.931
and he was dealing with it
pretty hard.

20:06.964 --> 20:09.434
Now, if anybody needs to talk
about what happened,

20:09.467 --> 20:12.102
please visit Mrs. Lindell
in the counselor's office.

20:12.136 --> 20:16.006
Mrs. Banks or any other teacher
will write you a pass.

20:16.040 --> 20:18.809
Thank you, Mrs. Banks.

20:25.216 --> 20:27.585
MRS. BANKS:
I think it's good to remember

20:27.618 --> 20:30.321
that we all have

20:30.355 --> 20:33.023
personal things going on
in our life

20:33.057 --> 20:34.825
that other people may not
know about.

20:36.694 --> 20:38.463
So...

20:38.496 --> 20:40.631
-Hi, Mrs. Banks.
-Oh, hello, Denisha.

20:43.601 --> 20:46.971
MRS. BANKS:
But... let's try to be

20:47.004 --> 20:49.173
more understanding
of one another.

20:51.208 --> 20:55.145
Okay, um, turn to page 45

20:55.179 --> 20:56.481
in your books.

20:56.514 --> 20:59.984
And, uh, who wants to read?

21:00.017 --> 21:02.520
-I'll do it, Mrs. Banks.
-Okay.

21:06.924 --> 21:09.193
Whenever you're ready.

21:18.035 --> 21:20.204
Hey.

21:20.237 --> 21:22.607
You look tired.

21:22.640 --> 21:25.175
No, I'm okay.
Just a long day.

21:25.209 --> 21:28.379
Maybe you need to start going to
bed sooner and stop staying up.

21:28.413 --> 21:31.382
Hey, Earn.
-Hey, Auntie.

21:31.416 --> 21:34.018
GLORIA:
I got a call from the school.

21:34.051 --> 21:36.754
One of your classmates died.

21:36.787 --> 21:38.689
-Yeah, Devin.
-Hmm.

21:38.723 --> 21:40.291
-Kind of.

21:40.325 --> 21:43.561
That's so sad.
She seemed to think

21:43.594 --> 21:45.430
maybe some of the older boys
were messing with him.

21:45.463 --> 21:50.167
You better say something
if somebody tries harassing you.

21:50.200 --> 21:52.169
People will bully you
your whole life if you let 'em.

21:52.202 --> 21:53.771
-Yeah, they will.
-You got to stand up
for yourself.

21:53.804 --> 21:54.772
Mm-hmm, and you and your cousin

21:54.805 --> 21:57.575
got to look out for each other.

21:57.608 --> 21:59.577
You guys look out
for each other, now.

21:59.610 --> 22:02.780
Boy, get your feet
out that chair.

22:02.813 --> 22:04.214
GLORIA: You start
piano lessons tomorrow.

22:04.248 --> 22:06.817
-Yeah, I'm ready.

22:06.851 --> 22:08.786
I'm gonna lay out
a suit for you,

22:08.819 --> 22:11.121
so you'll need to add
a black belt.

22:11.155 --> 22:12.757
A suit?
Why I got to wear that?

22:12.790 --> 22:14.559
Because I said so.

22:14.592 --> 22:15.893
You want to make
a good impression.

22:15.926 --> 22:17.462
Our mother always said,

22:17.495 --> 22:19.730
"You got one chance to make
a first impression."

22:19.764 --> 22:21.231
LORRAINE:
Mm-hmm. True indeed.

22:21.265 --> 22:23.033
But it's gonna be all hot...

22:23.067 --> 22:24.301
GLORIA:
I don't care.

22:24.335 --> 22:26.971
You are a black man in America,

22:27.004 --> 22:29.807
and when you meet people,
you need to look good.

22:29.840 --> 22:31.909
Your clothes are important.

22:31.942 --> 22:35.846
That's true, Earn.
You need to wear the suit.

22:39.450 --> 22:41.151
GLORIA:
Oh, and I got you another one

22:41.185 --> 22:42.787
of those FUBU shirts.

22:42.820 --> 22:44.422
It was on sale.

22:44.455 --> 22:47.324
Don't say I never did
anything for you.

22:47.358 --> 22:48.793
Thanks.

22:55.332 --> 22:58.002
* Ooh, ooh, ooh *

22:58.035 --> 23:00.304
* Ooh-ooh-ooh, ooh-ooh-ooh *

23:00.337 --> 23:03.207
* Ooh, ooh, ooh *

23:03.240 --> 23:04.609
* Ooh-ooh-ooh, ooh *

23:04.642 --> 23:05.743
* Ooh, ooh, ooh-ooh-ooh *

23:05.776 --> 23:08.479
* Life *

23:08.513 --> 23:10.114
* I wonder *

23:10.147 --> 23:12.783
* Will it take me under? *

23:12.817 --> 23:15.620
* I don't know *

23:15.653 --> 23:17.187
* Imagine smokin' weed
in the street *

23:17.221 --> 23:18.589
* Without cops harassin' *

23:18.623 --> 23:20.625
* Imagine goin' to court
with no trial *

23:20.658 --> 23:22.693
* Lifestyle:
cruisin' blue Bahama waters *

23:22.727 --> 23:24.662
* No welfare supporters,
more conscious of the way *

23:24.695 --> 23:26.163
* We raise our daughters *

23:26.196 --> 23:27.865
* Days are shorter,
nights are colder *

23:27.898 --> 23:29.500
* Feelin' like life is over *

23:29.534 --> 23:31.001
* These snakes strike
like a cobra *

23:31.035 --> 23:32.703
* The world's hot, my son
got knocked *

23:32.737 --> 23:34.472
* Evidently, it's elementary *

23:34.505 --> 23:35.806
* They want us all gone
eventually *

23:35.840 --> 23:38.142
* If I ruled the world *

23:38.175 --> 23:40.310
* Imagine that *

23:40.344 --> 23:43.481
* I'd free all my sons *

23:43.514 --> 23:46.183
* I love 'em, love 'em, baby *

23:46.216 --> 23:48.519
* Black diamonds and pearls *

23:51.388 --> 23:53.357
* If I ruled the world *

23:53.390 --> 23:57.361
* I love 'em, love 'em, baby. *

